<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:12:01Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Trump reportedly rejects Iran’s 7-day plan to reopen Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98066df5ab3899862405fe588b55a289d21800fc26bc44a319ae2690fa6e8e2a</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T02:06:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260926-trump-reportedly-rejects-iran-s-7-day-plan-to-reopen-strait-of-hormuz--f4edda057a7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260926-trump-reportedly-rejects-iran-s-7-day-plan-to-reopen-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump has reportedly rejected an Iranian plan to reopen the Strait of Hormuz. The proposal was presented by Iran's Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi to Trump’s envoy Steve Witkoff on the sidelines of a UN gathering in New York. The plan stipulated that the important waterway would reopen seven days after an agreement was reached.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV welcomed like a rock star at Stade de France near Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d52350926aefa2534ef079ef1ca6a0326d65856b564e8390d11828b92f6ae46d</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T21:06:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260925-pope-leo-xiv-welcomed-like-a-rock-star-at-stade-de-france-near-paris--8b14b2e06efc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260925-pope-leo-xiv-welcomed-like-a-rock-star-at-stade-de-france-near-paris" /><summary type="html">"For the pope, for God, make some noise!": Blending gospel and contemporary Christian music, 80,000 young Catholics filled the Stade de France on Friday evening to proclaim their faith. They gave Pope Leo XIV a rock-star welcome as he arrived at the stadium in his 'popemobile'.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen's president calls on his people to mobilise against Iran-backed Houthis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17ac863a55c3ee8d4b7166f75ed08244500e7c3b7f2d07b8fd14088fe72faa6e</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T20:41:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260925-yemen-president-calls-on-his-people-to-mobilise-against-iran-backed-houthis--89065aa49aef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260925-yemen-president-calls-on-his-people-to-mobilise-against-iran-backed-houthis" /><summary type="html">Yemen’s Riyadh-based President Rashid al-Alimi on Friday called on ‌his people to mobilise and join the armed ‌forces while offering a general amnesty to the Iran-backed Houthi rebels who have seized swaths of Yemen's Red Sea coast and imposed a naval blockade on Saudi Arabia.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Telecoms disruption raises fears as heavy fighting strikes Ethiopia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7322d4753c0a8e5eb1ffc7fba82aec9a958ca86b45fb6d27969265f54a0651a</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T20:32:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260925-telecoms-disruption-raises-fears-as-heavy-fighting-strikes-ethiopia--7d5d81c48ccb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20260925-telecoms-disruption-raises-fears-as-heavy-fighting-strikes-ethiopia" /><summary type="html">First, fighting continues between the Ethiopian forces and the Tigray People's Liberation Front as fears of a regional spillover continue to mount. Then, both the opposition and the ruling UDPS party continue to blame each other for the violence in the latest mass protest. And, the Authenticity and Modernity party looks now to form a coalition to address the top voter issues including the cost of living crisis in Morocco.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>‘I hope France wakes up’: Young Catholics flood the streets for Pope Leo's Paris visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e366b1e035d8f76086b4d1dc693abe7002e42decb379888e3cb04485b0746923</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T19:57:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260925-i-hope-france-wakes-up-young-catholics-flood-the-streets-for-pope-leo-s-paris-visit--8b0ca70f0bfd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260925-i-hope-france-wakes-up-young-catholics-flood-the-streets-for-pope-leo-s-paris-visit" /><summary type="html">Armed with paper fortune-tellers and pop worship songs, young French Catholics from the Anuncio movement fanned out into the crowds awaiting Pope Leo XIV's arrival in Paris on Friday, hoping to bring strangers closer to God in one of Europe's most secular countries.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Leo XIV in Paris: A look at the vespers evening prayer at Notre-Dame</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81ac215e25c16ad4d14553a56815bfc8ae422aa44fd7787a0d792de33122772f</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T19:46:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260925-leo-xiv-in-paris-a-look-at-the-vespers-evening-prayer-at-notre-dame--901aedcb49a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260925-leo-xiv-in-paris-a-look-at-the-vespers-evening-prayer-at-notre-dame" /><summary type="html">On Friday, Pope Leo XIV praised the "splendor" of Notre-Dame de Paris, which has been restored following the devastating fire of 2019, saying "the heart of a people" beats within this place. He is the first pope to visit the cathedral since its reopening in 2024.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope in Paris, Xi in DC, AI at a Crossroads</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd59dadd12baac0efc9ad1c88a5726e9e23beb33caa4e1a13d9d04e56c6d60f4</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T18:52:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260925-pope-in-paris-xi-in-dc-ai-at-a-crossroads--c82cbdb013fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260925-pope-in-paris-xi-in-dc-ai-at-a-crossroads" /><summary type="html">It’s been a week of walkouts, power plays and diplomatic theatre — from a battle over press freedom in Washington, to a United Nations General Assembly marked by protests and departures, as leaders clashed over Iran, Cuba and Venezuela. There was also a rare red-carpet meeting between Donald Trump and Xi Jinping, as the US and China extended their trade truce and turned their attention to the race for dominance in artificial intelligence. And from the geopolitical to the spiritual, Pope Leo brought his call for restraint and regulation of AI to France, as he sought to position the Vatican as a moral voice in a rapidly changing world.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Yemen's president calls on his people to mobilise against Iran-backed Houthis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee2c350f6514a7c2ee4c452d2a884d0c330e147bda10d50215fa77aea69d0b23</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:09:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T17:35:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-live-iran-s-president-says-us-must-choose-whether-to-end-war--8669e9479fa5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-live-iran-s-president-says-us-must-choose-whether-to-end-war" /></entry><entry><title>EU releases €6.6 billion for members arming Ukraine as seven killed in Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40f015e3c19e06ea974538decef04dd53fd9ef1ab9a1626a2b4a51a996f01d62</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T17:09:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-eu-releases-_6-6-billion-for-members-arming-ukraine-as-five-killed-in-kyiv--228cd20fb306.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-eu-releases-%E2%82%AC6-6-billion-for-members-arming-ukraine-as-five-killed-in-kyiv" /><summary type="html">European Union countries have agreed to release €6.6 billion from a fund meant to reimburse member states that have  provided arms to Ukraine, EU foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said on Friday. At least seven people were killed in Russian strikes on Kyiv earlier in the day, according to local authorities.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Lots of pomp but little progress as Trump and Xi end state visit to DC</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a035fa134caa82a60f65963e2977c77fd5e0656ac1b2e8a2289f104c2bf4ae3</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T16:58:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-lots-of-pomp-but-no-progress-as-trump-and-xi-end-state-visit--18a60b896000.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-lots-of-pomp-but-no-progress-as-trump-and-xi-end-state-visit" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump and Chinese leader Xi Jinping capped a state visit to Washington on Friday with pomp and pageantry but no real breakthroughs. Trump said he discussed the Iran war with Xi during his two-day visit, with both men confirming they will meet twice more before the end of the year.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Supreme Court allows Trump to use controversial voter 'verification' system</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1129b49ea15ae8881e26457376326cf588eca3e761f841c4575f301273763ffa</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T16:52:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-supreme-court-restores-trump-mass-voter-verification-system-despite-outcry--2eef72391964.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-supreme-court-restores-trump-mass-voter-verification-system-despite-outcry" /><summary type="html">The US Supreme Court on Friday ruled the Trump administration can use a controversial new federal database that would ostensibly verify voter citizenship in November’s elections. Critics argue the administration is exaggerating the threat of non-citizen voters – an extreme rarity in US elections – to implement policies that would disenfranchise likely Democratic voters.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leon XIV greets crowds on 'popemobile' ride through Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d424e3c3e8c37d6d1478c66aadf21538ca1b51f0ed3faf5d6ac4ba9411062f26</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T16:23:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260925-pope-leon-xiv-greets-crowds-on-popemobile-ride-through-paris--2862d8f046bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260925-pope-leon-xiv-greets-crowds-on-popemobile-ride-through-paris" /><summary type="html">Enthused believers hailed Pope Leo XIV as he waved to the crowds from a 'popemobile' in the French capital on Friday, after speeches calling for peace and warning against losing humanity in an AI-driven "paradise of machines". “He’s extraordinary”, said one person in the crowd just after the pope passed by.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV leads Vespers at Notre-Dame Cathedral in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eb744648175f5641cf53377c95d3310451b4bea23fe87b6212fb38a597f060cf</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T15:33:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-xiv-leads-vespers-at-notre-dame-cathedral-in-paris--7a4ed3866a5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-xiv-leads-vespers-at-notre-dame-cathedral-in-paris" /><summary type="html">Watch our special FRANCE 24 edition as Pope Leo XIV leads Vespers at Notre-Dame Cathedral on September 25 during his visit to Paris. Our journalists followed the event live from outside the cathedral, while guests joined us to analyse the significance of this key moment in the pontiff's four-day visit to France.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV rides through Paris in the popemobile to Notre-Dame</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9436d044abc77eadf2a7d0843e0807a9b2996a0eccb9a310450609e0bc3d7a75</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T15:23:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-xiv-rides-through-paris-in-the-popemobile-to-notre-dame--408479eb542d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-xiv-rides-through-paris-in-the-popemobile-to-notre-dame" /><summary type="html">Watch our special FRANCE 24 coverage of Pope Leo XIV's visit to Paris as the pontiff travelled through the French capital in the popemobile on his way to Notre-Dame Cathedral, where our journalist Claire Paccalin was reporting live. During the special edition, Father Michael Baggot, professor of theology, also analysed the images and explained why Pope Leo XIV has made transhumanism and the ethical challenges of artificial intelligence a recurring theme of his pontificate.</summary></entry><entry><title>America at 250: From the American dream to book bans and AI</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:859151af7cc9e2a1c57d0a95bdc7bd68453312ee8ad0627c282ac107539a428c</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T15:17:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260925-america-at-250-from-the-american-dream-to-book-bans-and-ai--f52dd805055d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260925-america-at-250-from-the-american-dream-to-book-bans-and-ai" /><summary type="html">As the United States marks its 250th anniversary, its founding promises, identity and place in the world are being fiercely debated. As the Festival America in Vincennes gets underway, we're putting that question to two acclaimed novelists: New Yorker Taffy Brodesser-Akner, author of "Long Island Compromise", and Lebanese-American writer Rabih Alameddine, whose novel "The True True Story of Raja the Gullible (and His Mother)" won the 2025 National Book Award for Fiction.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>EU vows to pursue €120 million fine on X after US backs Musk's court challenge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:904b4e50290861c5cf80d5b9ab4535b3e3e5f814ec9b7e427fa6239068a7059f</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T15:01:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-eu-vows-to-pursue-_120-million-fine-on-x-after-us-backs-musk-s-court-challenge--67ad47c60d3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-eu-vows-to-pursue-%E2%82%AC120-million-fine-on-x-after-us-backs-musk-s-court-challenge" /><summary type="html">The European Union on Friday said it will pursue a €120 million fine against the X social network after the US Justice Department said it supported the efforts of X owner Elon Musk to have the case annulled. The bloc fined the platform in 2025 for breaching EU online transparency rules, notably with its pay-to-play blue "verification" checkmark.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Pope Leo arrives at Notre-Dame after greeting crowds on 'popemobile' procession through Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38696e2df341bd550b0aba9e1f759f95c4c5ae5d44b17f31c46f549106326e50</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:09:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:55:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-live-pope-france-first-state-visit-18-years--58e532ec129c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260925-live-pope-france-first-state-visit-18-years" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Pope Leo XIV's address at UNESCO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f20427ea3c2aa680ca94f42e58923fba6b3f7a2be46b20499db7a4d63d6c9b17</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:54:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/replay-pope-leo-xiv-s-address-at-unesco--46ca2c7bd4b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/replay-pope-leo-xiv-s-address-at-unesco" /><summary type="html">Watch the replay of Pope Leo XIV's address at UNESCO on September 25, 2026 where he spoke about peace, culture, AI and international cooperation during the first stop of his France visit.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Moldova is the best performer in my class': EU Enlargement Commissioner Marta Kos</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60e6851186f9b99e645288a880b09c738e6be51ea204cc7dd102baf377534afd</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:54:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260925-moldova-is-the-best-performer-in-my-class-eu-enlargement-commissioner-marta-kos--14965558a28e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260925-moldova-is-the-best-performer-in-my-class-eu-enlargement-commissioner-marta-kos" /><summary type="html">The EU has gone through seven waves of enlargement since 1973, but there has not been one since Croatia joined in 2013. Indeed, there are not likely to be any new members in the club before 2028 – some 15 years after Croatia entered. But 2026 undeniably has momentum, and is on track to be a record year in terms of opening and closing new chapters for existing applicants. That is why our guest, EU Enlargement Commissioner Marta Kos, sees this as "the year of the enlargement."</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Climate breakdown: Is the EU adapting to the new normal? Europe's summer of disasters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f2e45771364b5042ffa2ad3683cbfcec5cc825d0ff9b138cdee1a809e86779b</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:33:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260925-climate-breakdown-is-the-eu-adapting-to-the-new-normal-europe-s-summer-of-disasters--f8e97073c504.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260925-climate-breakdown-is-the-eu-adapting-to-the-new-normal-europe-s-summer-of-disasters" /><summary type="html">It has been called Europe's disaster year. 2026 has seen more than 30,000 excess deaths linked to heatwaves, along with mega wildfires, nuclear power plants having to shut down, gas plants under pressure, droughts reducing hydropower generation from rivers and wild fluctuations in electricity prices, not to mention major disruptions to crops and farming in general.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Paris court convicts two for 2022 murder of Argentine rugby star Aramburu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:081a111bc78522552f34b984d334ce4ebd7058373af283d3cd255a01aec411ab</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:16:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260925-suspected-paris-killer-of-argentine-rugby-star-begs-forgiveness-from-victim-s-family--8a40fbfa9c65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260925-suspected-paris-killer-of-argentine-rugby-star-begs-forgiveness-from-victim-s-family" /><summary type="html">A Paris court on Friday sentenced the two main suspects in the 2022 murder of Argentine rugby player Federico Martin Aramburu to prison terms. Loik Le Priol, who fired the fatal shots, was sentenced to 26 years while Romain Bouvier, who fired first, was sentenced to 19 years. Both men had links to the far right.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>France: Pope Leo XIV keeps visit focused on faith over politics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c582eca7d65b922725f87f7b61918707c02787f90e41d3466c3a84915fe01b7c</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:08:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-pope-leo-xiv-keeps-visit-focused-on-faith-over-politics--20f0cf6a39c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-pope-leo-xiv-keeps-visit-focused-on-faith-over-politics" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV has declined a state dinner, the Legion of Honour and a private meeting with President Emmanuel Macron, keeping his four-day France visit centred on its apostolic mission despite official talks at the Élysée. While the Vatican cited scheduling reasons, some observers see a desire to emphasise the trip's spiritual focus, even as the pontiff is set to address European security and peace during his stop in Metz.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paris: Pope Leo XIV expected at UNESCO and Notre-Dame</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65e6fddd16c27f94121f57f6b810458d308d3a85291b73044d3828ebfeef3045</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:11:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:06:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/paris-pope-leo-xiv-expected-at-unesco-and-notre-dame--277ba0f8fc6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/paris-pope-leo-xiv-expected-at-unesco-and-notre-dame" /><summary type="html">Crowds have already begun gathering outside Notre-Dame Cathedral as Pope Leo XIV prepares for one of the highlights of his Paris visit. Before heading to the cathedral, the pontiff is expected to deliver another speech at UNESCO headquarters, where he is set to address global challenges including peace, culture and international cooperation, as FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Iran has dragged us into this conflict,' top Emirati diplomat Anwar Gargash says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d379e3359a335a7acbe81c78b4afba4c0dcfa89c0a2e30ccdac7bd997bb7c84d</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:12:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:04:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20260925-iran-has-dragged-us-into-this-conflict-top-emirati-diplomat-anwar-gargash-says--f3e23abd416a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260925-iran-has-dragged-us-into-this-conflict-top-emirati-diplomat-anwar-gargash-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24 on the sidelines of the UN General Assembly, Anwar Gargash, senior diplomatic adviser to the UAE president, said Iran "has dragged us into this conflict", after the UAE was "the target of 3,300 missiles and drones" fired by Iran. After US President Donald Trump said he could either negotiate with or "obliterate" Iran, Gargash warned that the "current situation of no war, no peace is not sustainable".</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry></feed>
